    "description": "Live 2026-10-17: PR #956 (fix for #952) merged 10:55Z with `Closes #952` as the first body line, but #952 stayed OPEN. Evidence: #952's timeline has only `referenced` events — no `cross-referenced` (the event GitHub creates when a closing keyword is parsed); #956's body updatedAt == mergedAt (10:55Z). Conclusion: the closing keyword was added to the body at/after the merge moment (finalize-step body rewrite), so GitHub never parsed it — closing keywords are evaluated on PR creation and body edits, and post-merge edits are too late. All six CRAP PRs the same morning auto-closed their issues normally — #956's lifecycle was atypical (rework leg died on push at 10:23Z, a later run finalized). Fix: the PR body (including the Closes keyword) must be final BEFORE the PR enters the merge queue; the finalize step must not rewrite the body after validation arms.\n\n## Machine jobs\n- [x] ▶ dev (fa-story-dev) · [run](https://github.com/IstiN/dmtools-agents/actions/runs/39049803156) · started 16:33 · done 16:46 ✅"
